  "tail_text": "diff` to apply unified diff patches.\n\nunicaa01_p58_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Apply unified diff patch to a string.\"\"\"\ndef apply_patch(text: str, patch: str) -> str:\n    lines = patch.splitlines()\n    # Parse hunk header and get old/new lines\n    # Expect format: \"@@ -1,1 +1,1 @@\\n-old\\n+new\"\n    hunk_start = next((i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.startswith('@@')), None)\n    if hunk_start is None:\n        return text\n    # Extract old and new from hunk: \"-old\" and \"+new\"\n    old_line = None\n    new_line = None\n    for line in lines[hunk_start+1:]:\n        if line.startswith('-') and not line.startswith('--'):\n            old_line = line[1:]\n        elif line.startswith('+') and not line.startswith('++'):\n            new_line = line[1:]\n        if old_line is not None and new_line is not None:\n            break\n    if old_line is None or new_line is None:\n        return text\n    # Replace first occurrence of old_line with new_line\n    if text == old_line:\n        return new_line\n    # For multi-line text, replace first occurrence (simple)\n    return text.replace(old_line, new_line, 1)\n\ndef demo():\n    p = \"@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-foo\\n+bar\"\n    return apply_patch(\"foo\", p)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(demo())\n```",
  "full_completion_text": "diff` to apply unified diff patches.\n\nunicaa01_p58_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Apply unified diff patch to a string.\"\"\"\ndef apply_patch(text: str, patch: str) -> str:\n    lines = patch.splitlines()\n    # Parse hunk header and get old/new lines\n    # Expect format: \"@@ -1,1 +1,1 @@\\n-old\\n+new\"\n    hunk_start = next((i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if line.startswith('@@')), None)\n    if hunk_start is None:\n        return text\n    # Extract old and new from hunk: \"-old\" and \"+new\"\n    old_line = None\n    new_line = None\n    for line in lines[hunk_start+1:]:\n        if line.startswith('-') and not line.startswith('--'):\n            old_line = line[1:]\n        elif line.startswith('+') and not line.startswith('++'):\n            new_line = line[1:]\n        if old_line is not None and new_line is not None:\n            break\n    if old_line is None or new_line is None:\n        return text\n    # Replace first occurrence of old_line with new_line\n    if text == old_line:\n        return new_line\n    # For multi-line text, replace first occurrence (simple)\n    return text.replace(old_line, new_line, 1)\n\ndef demo():\n    p = \"@@ -1 +1 @@\\n-foo\\n+bar\"\n    return apply_patch(\"foo\", p)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(demo())\n```",
